  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The amplitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;is modulated by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> signal. The amplitude modulated signal contains frequency (ies) of</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>498</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>502</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "A only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A, D and E only",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "B only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A and B only",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The frequency components of amplitude modulated signal are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></math></p><p>Here, carrier wave frequency is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>Modulating wave frequency is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>So, the frequencies in amplitude modulated signal are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>498</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>502</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p>"
  }
}